  But as has been pointed out before, the way Nethack uses the 
RNG is almost like an RNG itself.  Previous random events affect
later random events.  That's why two players starting with the
same game saved on turn 1 will have very different dungeons.

  So even a Predictable Number Generator (and they all are, 
really.  "Anyone who attempts to generate random numbers by 
deterministic means is, of course, living in a state of sin." -
John von Neumann) could look good when used by Nethack.

  Perhaps a separate seed for the dungeon levels would permit
multiple players to compete in playing the same dungeon layout? 
(That's been tried before but using wizard mode to visit every
level first, then tweaking the save file.)

